  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, funded by the Government of Denmark, will ensure speedy reconstruction of critical health care facilities in the city and region of Mykolaiv, Ukraine to facilitate uninterrupted provision of critical health care services throughout the oblast. Direct beneficiaries include 1,769 hospital personnel and up to 90,500 patients. Indirect beneficiaries encompass approximately 1.1 million inhabitants of Mykolaiv Oblast (based on 2022 estimates), potentially extending to the entire population of Ukraine, given Ukrainian legislation guarantees medical services regardless of residency status.</narrative>
   </title>
